Why the license file contains the license text and nothing else: automated
license detectors (including the one in this repository) identify a project's
license by matching the file against canonical texts. Prepending a copyright
header to a license body causes GitHub to report "Other" instead of
"AGPL-3.0", which makes the project's licensing look unclear to exactly the
audience that cares about it. The notice therefore lives here.

Third-party license texts in tests/fixtures/ are reproduced verbatim from the
GitHub Licenses API and the SPDX License List (spdx/license-list-data) so that
the test suite asserts against the real documents. They remain under their own
licenses.

Third-party SBOM documents in tests/fixtures/sbom/ are reproduced from:

  - CycloneDX/bom-examples, SBOM/juice-shop/v11.1.2/bom.json (CC0-1.0). Only a
    subset of its component objects is committed, unmodified, so the fixture
    keeps the mixed SPDX-id / expression / name-only / absent license shapes
    that make real BOMs hard to read.
  - spdx/spdx-examples, software/example11/spdx2.3/sbom.spdx.json and
    software/example1/spdx3.0/example1.spdx3.json. Both are committed whole and
    unmodified; the second is the fixture that proves SPDX 3.0 license
    expressions are reached through relationships rather than package fields.

Those repositories' own licenses are GPL-3.0 and CC0-1.0 respectively; the test
data is used as data, and its provenance is recorded here so that a reader can
